hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24291","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Zuhayr ibn Qays al-Balawi, from Alqamah ibn Rimthah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Amr ibn al-As to al-Bahrayn, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a detachment, and we went out with him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dozed. So he said: May Allah have mercy on Amr. He said: So we discussed everyone whose name is Amr. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dozed and said: May Allah have mercy on Amr. He said: Then he dozed a third time and woke up and said: May Allah have mercy on Amr. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, which Amr is this? He said: Amr ibn al-As. We said: And what is his matter? He said: Whenever I urged the people to charity, he would come and give generously from it. So I would say: O Amr, whence do you have this? He would say: From Allah. And Amr has spoken the truth; he has much good with Allah. Zuhayr ibn Qays said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, I said: I shall keep to this one of whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has much good with Allah, until I die."
